Helper: AllocateAndBindMemory sorts every buffer and every texture of a group.

HelperDeviceMemoryAllocator::GroupByMemoryType sorts each kind by memory type, then ascending
alignment, before packing, but passes &buffers[bufferNum - 1] and &textures[textureNum - 1] as the
end of the range, which std::sort excludes: the last buffer and the last texture are packed where
they were passed, and two of a kind are never sorted. Since b5e2b07.

This sorts the whole range.
Measured on v190, NVIDIA: Vulkan buffers aligned to 128, 64 and 16 passed as scratch, constant,
vertex landed at +1024, +0, +2032. Three buffers of 1,008 B at 16, 1,024 B at 64 and 1,008 B at 128
(3,056 B packed in ascending alignment), with preferredMemorySize 3,056, needed two allocations in 2
of the 6 orders; on D3D12, textures of 16 KiB and 4 KiB at 4 KiB and 64 KiB at 64 KiB (128 KiB packed)
needed two in the 4 orders that put a 4 KiB one last. With the change every order packs into one
allocation, on both backends.

